\code{\link[=as_ggseg_atlas]{as_ggseg_atlas()}} rebuilds the atlas through the current constructor,
which fills in whatever is new and revalidates against current rules.

This matters because atlases are published, not just made: roughly 150 of
them live in \code{R/sysdata.rda} files across the atlas packages, each built by
whichever \code{ggseg.formats} was current that day, and r-universe rebuilds
